<article class="env-lemma" id="03V8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03V8">Lemma <span data-tag="03V8">64.23.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a smooth, projective, geometrically irreducible curve over a finite field $k$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the $L$-function $L(X, \mathbf{Q}_\ell )$ is a rational function, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the eigenvalues $\alpha _1, \ldots , \alpha _{2g}$ of $\pi _ X^*$ on $H^1(X_{\bar k}, \mathbf{Q}_\ell )$ are algebraic integers independent of $\ell $, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the number of rational points of $X$ on $k_ n$, where $[k_ n : k] = n$, is 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \#  X(k_ n) = 1 - \sum \nolimits _{i = 1}^{2g}\alpha _ i^ n + q^ n,  \]
</div>
</li><li><p>
for each $i$, $|\alpha _ i| < q$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (3) is Theorem <a href="/tag/03V2" data-tag="03V2">64.20.5</a> applied to $\mathcal{F} = \underline{\mathbf{Q}_\ell }$ on $X \otimes k_ n$. For part (4), use the following result. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>